  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "Atlas, database and modeling reports this period tie omics data to disease context, from a 12.6M-cell atlas to kinase mutation–drug response.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is integration of heterogeneous molecular data into disease-contextualized, queryable resources with built-in analysis. PANGEA remaps 12.6M cells into a 32-type, 165-subtype hierarchy to profile multicellular responses across 160 diseases. KinaseMD 2.0 links kinase mutations to inhibitor response and phosphorylation signaling. A 1,824-tumor lung RNA-seq cohort defines nine transcriptional clusters tied to histology, genetics, immunity and survival, with an interactive component. Several items contribute analytical frameworks rather than databases: CellChat Hotspot adds gene-set enrichment and filtering to cell-cell communication inference, spatial causal discovery is applied to Visium liver data, a natural-product atlas uses PPI networks and signed random walks across nine cancers, and multi-omics-constrained kinetic models predict 28 enzyme vulnerabilities in BRCA1-deficient ovarian cancer.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
